### META
directory_path: install
last_updated: 2025-11-28T14:42:00Z
description: Main installation directory containing the orchestrators (setup.sh, webui.sh) and all installation-related components including Manifests, function modules, validators, Docker configurations, and CLI tools.
notes: This directory contains both the base installer (_setup.sh/) and the WebUI installer (_webui.sh/).
---

### FILE
file_name: setup.sh
file_type: script
language_or_format: bash
role: Main installer orchestrator that reads the Manifest, parses sections and operations, resolves placeholders, loads modules and validators, and dispatches installation operations.
used_by:
  - dinser setup command
  - Manual installation
depends_on:
  - _setup.sh/Manifest
  - _setup.sh/_*.sh modules
  - _setup.sh/_validate_*.sh validators
status: active
notes: Core orchestrator with no hard-coded install logic.

functions:
  - name: main
    kind: function
    purpose: Entry point that orchestrates the entire installation process by reading and executing the Manifest.
    usage_examples:
      - sudo ./install/setup.sh
      - DEBUG=1 sudo ./install/setup.sh
      - sudo ./install/setup.sh --dry-run
    parameters:
      - name: --dry-run
        type: bool
        required: false
        default: "false"
        description: Parse Manifest without executing operations.
        allowed_values:
          - none
      - name: --manifest
        type: path
        required: false
        default: "_setup.sh/Manifest"
        description: Path to alternate Manifest file.
        allowed_values:
          - none
      - name: --max-phase
        type: int
        required: false
        default: none
        description: Stop after specified phase number.
        allowed_values:
          - none
    returns:
      type: int
      description: Exit code (0=success, 1=config error, 2=runtime error).
    side_effects:
      - Creates directories and files as specified in Manifest
      - Modifies system configuration
      - Installs DINSER CLI
      - Sets up Docker Swarm
    errors:
      - condition: Manifest parse error
        behavior: Logs error and exits with code 1
      - condition: Module not found
        behavior: Logs error, marks step as failed, continues
    messages:
      - type: stdout
        content: Progress and status messages for each section/operation
      - type: log
        content: Detailed execution logs with timestamps
---

### FILE
file_name: webui.sh
file_type: script
language_or_format: bash
role: WebUI installer orchestrator that manages the Docker-based setup WebUI including building, starting, stopping, and status checking.
used_by:
  - dinser webui command
  - Manual WebUI management
depends_on:
  - _webui.sh/Manifest
  - _webui.sh/docker/docker-compose.webui.yml
  - _webui.sh/docker/Dockerfile.webui
status: active
notes: Wrapper for Docker Compose operations specific to the WebUI.

functions:
  - name: main
    kind: function
    purpose: Entry point that dispatches WebUI management commands.
    usage_examples:
      - ./install/webui.sh manifest
      - ./install/webui.sh up
      - ./install/webui.sh down
      - ./install/webui.sh status
    parameters:
      - name: command
        type: enum
        required: true
        default: none
        description: Command to execute.
        allowed_values:
          - manifest
          - up
          - down
          - status
          - restart
          - logs
          - build
          - shell
          - config-path
    returns:
      type: int
      description: Exit code from Docker Compose or command execution.
    side_effects:
      - Starts/stops Docker containers
      - Creates configuration directories
      - Builds Docker images
    errors:
      - condition: Docker not available
        behavior: Exits with error message
      - condition: Container build failure
        behavior: Logs error and exits with non-zero code
    messages:
      - type: stdout
        content: Container status and command output
---

### DIRECTORIES
subdirectories:
  - name: _setup.sh
    path: install/_setup.sh
    role: Contains the base installer engine including Manifest, function modules (_mkdir.sh, _copy.sh, etc.), validators (_validate_*.sh), CLI tools (dinser), and Docker configurations.
  - name: _webui.sh
    path: install/_webui.sh
    role: Contains the WebUI engine including its Manifest, FastAPI backend with modular sections, frontend with modular pages, Docker configurations, and Nginx settings.
---
